      "statusChangeNewStatus": "closed",
      "value": "Already left this comment on Discord, but will comment here while closing for record visibility, etc.\nAnything that doesn't write to the depth texture will not be properly blurred.\nDepth of Field works on the depth texture. Transparent shaders or shaders that do not have a shadowcaster pass do not write to the depth texture, so they will be blurred as if they are at the distance of the nearest thing behind the object that does write to depth. They are effectively invisible as far as the camera DoF system is concerned.\nTLDR; \nThis is a Unity limitation, and not something we can fix on our end.\nDon't use shaders that don't write to depth.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
